{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.TemperleyLiebTower","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTowerBasicConstruction","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Module.LinearMap.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.TwoSidedIdeal.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.TwoSidedIdeal.Operations"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.heckeBraidedPresentationOfRank_quot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.heckeBraidedPresentationOfRank_quot","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L257-L299","doc":"**The braided presentation descends to the quotient.**\n\nEvery relation of `HeckeBraidedPresentationOfRank` holds for the images of the\ngenerators, at the same rank. The proof is `map_mul` / `map_smul` / `map_one`\nunder the algebra hom — the content is that such a hom exists at all, which is\nthe instance above.\n\nWhat this does **not** do: it does not produce a `WenzlTowerStep` instance at\nthe Markov trace. That additionally needs the tower inclusion `Hn →ₐ Hn1` shown\nto descend compatibly with the two radicals, which is brick 3 and is not\nautomatic — the radicals at consecutive ranks are different ideals in different\nalgebras, and nothing here relates them.\n\n🛑 Measured 2026-09-27: **nothing in the corpus consumes `WenzlTowerStep`** — 27\noccurrences, of which 1 class definition, 2 discharge targets and 24 prose mentions,\nand **zero** instance-hypothesis positions. So an instance unblocks no consumer, and\nat a Hecke carrier its conclusion is free outright\n(`isSemisimpleRing_hecke_generic`; see\n`QOU.Machinery.HeckeRank.wenzlTowerStep_vacuous_of_isSemisimpleRing`). The sentence\nabove is kept as the record of what this file did not do; read it as naming an open\nquestion, not a live blocker. Bean `qou-s7z2`.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quotMk_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quotMk_apply","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L251-L255","doc":"Deliberately NOT `@[simp]`: marking it so lets `simp` strip the algebra-hom\nwrapper, which breaks the `hecke_quadratic` descent — the `•` is then stranded\ninside the quotient map. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quotMk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quotMk","kind":"def","line":241,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L241-L249","doc":"**The quotient map, as an algebra hom.** This is the object the descent\nneeds; `RingCon.mk'` alone is too weak because it does not move `•`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.instAlgebraTraceQuot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.instAlgebraTraceQuot","kind":"instance","line":229,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L229-L239","doc":"**The quotient is an `R`-algebra.** Centrality of `algebraMap`'s image is\ninherited from `A`: reduce to a representative and apply `Algebra.commutes`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quot_pairing_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quot_pairing_one","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L186-L190","doc":"**And the pairing genuinely separates that class**, rather than the\nexistential being satisfied by an unreachable witness: `τ̄(1̄ · 1̄) = τ 1 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quot_one_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quot_one_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L178-L184","doc":"**Non-vacuity guard: the quotient is not the zero ring** when `τ 1 ≠ 0`.\nWithout this, `quot_pairing_nondegenerate` would be satisfiable by collapsing\neverything to `0`. The Markov trace is normalised with `τ 1 = 1`, so the\nhypothesis holds in the intended application. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.one_not_mem_traceRadical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.one_not_mem_traceRadical","kind":"theorem","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L173-L176","doc":"**The unit is outside the radical whenever `τ 1 ≠ 0`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quot_pairing_nondegenerate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quot_pairing_nondegenerate","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L142-L162","doc":"**The descended pairing is non-degenerate — in the shape `WenzlTowerStep`\nasks for.**\n\n`WenzlTowerStep.semisimple_ascend` wants its trace to satisfy\n`∀ y ≠ 0, ∃ z, tr (y * z) ≠ 0`. On `H_n` at convention D that is **false**\n(`MarkovGramDegenerate.gram_det_eq_zero_of_radical_combination`). Here it holds,\nfor the descended trace on the quotient, and the proof is short because the\nradical was quotiented out by construction: a nonzero class is a non-radical\nelement, and a non-radical element is by definition one the pairing separates.\n\nThe content is not the argument; it is that the statement now has a *quotient\nring* to be about, rather than a congruence on `A`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quot_eq_zero_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quot_eq_zero_iff","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L136-L140","doc":"**A class vanishes exactly on the radical.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quotTrace_mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quotTrace_mk","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L132-L134","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quotTrace","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.quotTrace","kind":"def","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L121-L130","doc":"**The trace, descended to the quotient.** Well defined because related\nelements differ by a radical element, which the trace kills. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.TraceQuot","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.TraceQuot","kind":"def","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L117-L119","doc":"**The quotient `A / rad τ`.** For the Markov trace on `H_n(q)` at convention\nD this is the object the corpus calls `TL_n(δ)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.traceRadical_apply_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.traceRadical_apply_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L106-L113","doc":"**The radical sits inside the kernel of the trace.** Take `b = 1`: an\nelement pairing to zero against *everything* pairs to zero against the unit.\nThis is the step that needs `A` unital, and it is what lets the trace descend\nto the quotient rather than merely the pairing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.mem_traceRadicalIdeal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.mem_traceRadicalIdeal","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L93-L99","doc":"**Membership in the ideal is membership in the radical**, definitionally\nthrough `mk'`. Stated so downstream proofs never unfold `mk'`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.traceRadicalIdeal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.traceRadicalIdeal","kind":"def","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L78-L91","doc":"**The trace radical, as a two-sided ideal.**\n\nThe object the phrase `H_n / rad τ` needs in order to denote anything. Assembled\nfrom the three additive closures above and the two multiplicative closures in\n`TemperleyLiebTower`; `hcyc` (trace cyclicity) is consumed by exactly one of the\nfive, `traceRadical_mem_mul`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.traceRadical_neg_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.traceRadical_neg_mem","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L72-L76","doc":"**The radical is closed under negation.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.traceRadical_add_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.traceRadical_add_mem","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L65-L70","doc":"**The radical is closed under addition.** `τ((x+y)·b) = τ(x·b) + τ(y·b)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.traceRadical_zero_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.MarkovTraceQuotient.traceRadical_zero_mem","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/MarkovTraceQuotient.lean#L59-L63","doc":"**`0` is in the radical.** `τ(0 · b) = τ(0) = 0` by linearity. ","signatureChunk":0}]}